  <!-- ==================== The settings file (RealGlass.xml) ==================== -->
  <!-- Comments the mod writes into the player's settings file. The names of the settings in
       that file are not translated. -->

  <!-- One line of the file per \n: a bullet wrapped here stays one line there. -->
  <String key="File.Header">
    Real Glass settings.\n
    \n
    You can edit this file while the game is running: the mod reads it again within a
    second of it being saved, and the panels follow.\n
    \n
    - Numbers use a dot for decimals: 0.5, never 0,5.\n
    - A percentage is written the way its slider shows it: 47 means 47%.\n
    - A value outside its range is pulled back into it. A value that cannot be read, and a
    name the mod does not know, are ignored. RealGlass.log says which.\n
    - A setting whose line is missing keeps the value it has (at startup, its default).\n
    - If the file cannot be read at all, the mod leaves it alone and says so in the log.\n
    - The mod rewrites this file, these comments included, whenever a setting changes in
    the game: notes of your own will not survive.\n
    - Delete the file with the game closed to start again from every default.
  </String>
  <String key="File.Section.Panel">In-game panel: {0} tab</String>
  <String key="File.Section.Options">The game's options page</String>
  <String key="File.Section.None">Not shown on either page</String>
  <String key="File.Percent">{0}, in %. {1} to {2}, default {3}.</String>
  <String key="File.Number">{0}. {1} to {2}{3}, default {4}.</String>
  <String key="File.AnyNumber">{0}. Default {1}.</String>
  <String key="File.Readout">(slider: {0} to {1})</String>
  <String key="File.Toggle">{0}. true or false, default {1}.</String>
  <String key="File.Choice">{0}. One of {1}; default {2}.</String>
  <String key="File.Key">{0}. A key such as F8 or Ctrl+Shift+G, or None; default {1}.</String>
  <String key="File.Colour">{0}. A color, #RRGGBB (42, 92, 120 is read too); default {1}.</String>
  <String key="File.Confirm">Switching it on here skips the question the game asks first.</String>

  <!-- ==================== The assets file (RealGlassAssets.xml) ==================== -->

  <!-- One line of the file per \n. -->
  <String key="AssetFile.Header">
    Real Glass: the glass each building asset has of its own, on every copy of it, in every
    city. Nothing of it is kept in your saves.\n
    \n
    One Asset element per asset, holding only what it does not take from RealGlass.xml, under
    the same names and in the same units:\n
    - a percentage the way its slider shows it: 47 means 47%; GlassThreshold goes from 10 to 95
    (lower than in RealGlass.xml: it is this asset's alone);\n
    - GlassColor as #RRGGBB; GlassNightWindows as true or false;\n
    - GlassPreset as the number of a kind of glass (0 Custom, 1 to 10, as in RealGlass.xml);
    a kind of glass alone gives its color, reflectivity and clarity.\n
    \n
    The building window writes this file (press the building picker's key and click a
    building). You can edit it while the game is running too: the mod reads it again within a
    second. Take an asset's element out, or delete the file with the game closed, and it has
    the global glass again.
  </String>

